### High-contrast (`data-theme="high-contrast"`)
Pure black `#000` bg, pure white fg, yellow `#FFD700` brand/focus, no
translucency, 2px borders. Keep every rule ≥7:1.

Type tokens: `--font-display: Literata` (variable, incl. italic; self-hosted
TTF like the current fonts, with fallback faces), `--font-body: Manrope`
(variable), `--font-mono: DM Mono` (keep). Fluid display scale:
`--text-hero: clamp(2.75rem, 2rem + 3.5vw, 5rem)` etc. Keep
`--header-height` (may change value, keep the var). Keep radius/spacing var
names; radii soften: sm 6 / md 10 / lg 16 / xl 24.

## 3. Design language

- **Headlines:** Literata, weight 550–620, tight leading, `-0.015em`;
  `<em>` inside CMS titles renders as Literata *italic* in gold (`.hero-title
  em` etc. — the CMS content already carries `<em>` markup; make italic+gold
  the house style for it).
- **Kickers/eyebrows:** Manrope 700, 12–13px, +0.16em tracking, uppercase,
  gold.
- **Body:** Manrope, 17–18px base (respects A/A+/A++ root sizing), 1.65
  leading, max 68ch.
- **Numerals** (stats, 01/02 rows): Literata, oversized, tabular.
- **Surfaces:** flat night; elevation = `--bg-elevated` + gold hairline top
  or 1px border, almost no shadows on dark (shadows read on Day theme only).
- **Cards:** radius-lg, bg-elevated, 1px border, hover: border-strong +
  translateY(-2px). No glassmorphism except the nav bar.
- **Buttons:** pill. Primary = gold fill, night text (AA: #16121E on #E8A33D),
  hover brighter. Secondary = 1px gold outline, gold text. Quiet = underline.
  ≥48px targets. Focus ring 3px `--focus-ring` (keep existing focus system).
- **Links:** gold, underline on hover; in body text always underlined.
- **Motion:** existing Reveal component; 400–500ms rises, stagger ≤80ms;
  ripple arcs may breathe (6s) behind heroes; all gated by existing
  prefers-reduced-motion handling.
- **Imagery (when generated):** duotone night/gold grade; photos warm,
  dignified, never pity-framed. Until real imagery lands, sections use
  ripple/braille motifs — no stock, no placeholders.

## 4. Shell

- **Nav:** slim translucent night bar (backdrop-blur), gold logo
  (LogoAnimated inherits --brand/--accent — keep component), active link =
  gold text + 2px gold underline offset; A/A+/A++ and theme controls restyled
  as compact pill group; Donate = primary gold pill. Keep
  `--header-height` var + skip link.
- **Footer:** deepest night (#0B0A10), the Rumi line set huge in Literata
  italic as the footer's opening statement ("We are all blind until we see
  each other's pain."), then the existing link columns (all CMS/footer data
  kept), EIN/small print. Gold hairline top.
- **Subnav tabs:** underline tabs (no boxes), sticky under nav (keep
  `top: var(--header-height)`).

## 5. Pages (restructure freely; every CMS field keeps rendering)

- **Home:** hero = night sky with slow echo-ripple field radiating from a
  gold point (the eye opens), kicker + CMS heroTitle (em→gold italic) + sub +
  CTAs; impact strip → gold hairline row of Literata numerals; values →
  numbered editorial rows; projects grid → editorial cards with status chips;
  stories/timeline → keep data, restyle as archive rows; quote CTA band →
  full-bleed gold-on-night statement.
- **About:** FAQ 01–05 as oversized-numeral accordion rows; mission section
  with big Rumi pull-quote; team as portrait-initial tiles (gold monogram on
  night); founder's series as book-index rows (Literata italic titles).
- **Projects:** hero + cards with status ribbons restyled as gold corner
  tags; project detail pages restyled via their existing classes.
- **Media:** tabs; photo grid tiles (empty-state copy stays); podcast
  featured + guest form; video cards with duotone thumbs + category chips.
- **Documents:** research cards, newsletter band, stories, Book tab as an
  actual "book" — chapter list with big Literata numerals and italic titles.
- **Volunteers:** stats row, role cards → two-column editorial list with
  meta chips, steps → numbered vertical timeline, form restyled (all fields,
  validation, char counter, required-field a11y signalling kept).
- **Donate:** amount widget restyled (gold), impact breakdown as hairline
  rows, transparency section as flat editorial; "no payment taken" notice
  stays prominent.
- **Privacy/[slug]/detail pages:** `.prose` and `lib/pages/*` classes
  restyled; server-HTML contracts untouched.
- **Coming-soon/confirmed/404/500:** night + ripple + Literata statement.
- **TE assistant panel + audio tour overlay + mini player:** restyle to
  night/gold (the tour overlay's red becomes gold/night; keep all IDs,
  roles, and window.* contracts).

## 6. Hard contracts (do not break — from the architecture audit)

1. `getContent()` / field names / `visibleSorted` / `projects→programs`
   fallback.
2. Every page keeps `generateMetadata()` → `readSeoOverrides` + JsonLd.
3. RichText inline-tag allowlist; HtmlContent server-HTML injection;
   `lib/pages/*` class hooks restyled, not removed.
4. VoiceAssistant: `main h1/h2` + `main p` must exist per route; PAGES alias
   map; `#te-panel`; `window.setTheme`/audio-tour globals.
5. Theme keys `teww-theme`/`teww-size`, pre-paint script, `data-theme` +
   `data-text-size` attributes, ThemeProvider/NavProvider shell.
6. `--header-height` var consumed by subnav/scroll-padding.
7. `/ad-min` (AdminNav, admin.css, CMS density vars `--row-y --pad-card
   --gap --rail-w`) untouched and unbroken — tokens it shares must keep
   working in all three themes.
8. WCAG 2.2 AA minimum everywhere; the high-contrast theme targets AAA.
   State never by color alone; all existing aria/roles/labels preserved.

## 7. CSS architecture (set in the foundation PR)

`app/globals.css` becomes an ordered import manifest of `app/styles/*.css`:
`tokens.css` (fonts+themes) · `base.css` (reset, type, buttons, forms,
utilities) · `shell.css` (nav, footer, subnav, skip) · `home.css` ·
`about.css` · `projects.css` · `media.css` · `documents.css` ·
`volunteers.css` · `donate.css` · `pages.css` (prose, detail, coming-soon,
errors) · `assistant.css` (TE panel, tour, mini-player) · `cms-bridge.css`
(vars/classes ad-min depends on). Page PRs own exactly their file.
